  "system": {
    "description": {
      "gm": "",
      "value": "<p class=\"MsoNormal\">You try to wrench your target’s ether from their body. You either make a spell attack or force the target to make a basic saving throw, based on your chosen defense when you learned this cantrip. This cantrip gains the attack trait if you target a creature’s AC, and gains the tradition of your choice based on your selection when you learn this cantrip.</p><p class=\"MsoNormal\">On a hit or a failed saving throw, the target takes 1d4 spirit damage and loses a focus point. If you miss or the target succeeds, the target takes half damage. If the target has no focus points to drain, they take no damage, regardless of the outcome.</p><p class=\"MsoNormal\">If the target loses a focus point, you acquire a @UUID[Compendium.immortal-ardor.feats.cN0RefdXwBD9KgoF]{Effect: Mote of Ether}. You can then choose to absorb it as hit points, recovering hit points equal to half the amount of damage dealt or to absorb it as a focus point, granting you one focus point. Once a target loses a focus point, you cannot acquire a mote of ether from them again for 24 hours.</p><hr><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><strong>Heightened(+1)</strong>: Damage for this spell increases by 1d4.</p>"
    },
